    intro="Scrum techniques are the practices teams add to the Scrum framework to carry out the work it defines, such as user stories, planning poker, burndown charts, swarming and the Five Whys. The 2020 Scrum Guide is purposefully incomplete: it sets out the events, artifacts and accountabilities, and leaves the techniques to you. This guide explains 20 widely used Scrum techniques, which problem each one solves, how to use it step by step and how to choose the right ones for your team.",
